<%- include('../partials/head') %>

<%- include('../partials/breadcrumbs') %>

<div class="pagehead">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h1>Compliance and eligibility in Texas</h1>
    <p>Who may buy from this catalogue under federal and Texas law, and what is checked before a firearm is released.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="section">
  <div class="wrap prose">
    <h2>Age limits</h2>
    <p>
      This shop is a licensed dealer in the state of Texas, so federal age law applies at the counter. A handgun,
      a handgun frame or a handgun receiver may be transferred by a licensed dealer only to a buyer aged
      <%= jurisdiction.minimumAgeHandgun %> or over. A rifle or a shotgun may be transferred to a buyer aged
      <%= jurisdiction.minimumAgeLongGun %> or over. Parts, slides, triggers and accessories that are not
      themselves a firearm may be sold to a buyer aged <%= jurisdiction.minimumAgeAccessory %> or over.
    </p>
    <p>
      You are asked to confirm your age before an order request can be submitted. That confirmation is not
      the check. Age is verified against government issued photographic identification in person, before
      anything is handed over.
    </p>

    <h2>Prohibited persons</h2>
    <p>
      Federal law at 18 U.S.C. section 922(g) bars certain people from receiving or possessing a firearm.
      The categories include a person convicted of a crime punishable by more than one year in prison, a
      fugitive from justice, an unlawful user of a controlled substance, a person adjudicated as mentally
      defective or committed to a mental institution, a person subject to a qualifying protective order, a
      person convicted of a misdemeanor crime of domestic violence, and a person who is unlawfully in the
      United States. If any of those apply to you, you cannot lawfully buy a firearm here. Making a false
      statement on the federal transaction record is itself a felony.
    </p>

    <h2>The background check</h2>
    <p>
      Every firearm transfer from this dealer runs through <%= jurisdiction.transactionRecordForm %>, the
      federal firearms transaction record, completed by the buyer at the counter. The dealer then queries the
      <%= jurisdiction.backgroundCheckSystem %>. The system returns proceed, delay or deny. The firearm is
      released only on a proceed result. A delay result means the transfer waits until the check is resolved.
    </p>
    <p>
      Texas does not operate a separate state check. It defers to the federal system, and it adds no state
      purchase permit, no state waiting period and no state firearm registry. Do not read that as a shortcut:
      the federal check still happens on every transfer, every time.
    </p>

    <h2>Buying from outside Texas</h2>
    <p>
      Federal law limits a licensed dealer to selling a handgun face to face only to a resident of the
      dealer's own state. If you live outside Texas and you buy a handgun here, it is shipped to a licensed
      dealer in your state and you complete the transfer there, under the rules of your state. A rifle or a
      shotgun may be sold to an out of state resident where the sale is lawful in both states.
    </p>

    <h2>Your local law still governs you</h2>
    <p>
      Texas does not restrict magazine capacity, does not maintain an approved handgun roster and does not
      impose an assault weapon ban. Many other states do. An item appearing in this catalogue is not a
      statement that it is legal where you live. Checking the law of your own city and state is your
      responsibility, and this shop refuses any order it cannot lawfully complete.
    </p>

    <h2>How a firearm reaches you</h2>
    <% if (transferConfirmed) { %>
      <p><%= business.policy.transferProcessText %></p>
    <% } %>
    <p>The full route, including who pays which fee, is set out in the <a href="/shipping-and-transfer-policy">shipping and transfer policy</a>.</p>

    <h2>Orders this shop will not fill</h2>
    <% if (restricted.length) { %>
      <ul><% restricted.forEach(function (d) { %><li><%= d %></li><% }); %></ul>
    <% } %>

    <h2>Export</h2>
    <p>
      Firearms and many firearm parts are export controlled under United States law. Nothing in this
      catalogue is offered for export unless this shop states so in writing for that specific order, with the
      licences that permit it.
    </p>

    <h2>This page is not legal advice</h2>
    <p>
      This page describes how the shop operates and summarises the rules it works under. It is a summary,
      not legal advice about your own position, and the law changes. If you are unsure whether you may
      lawfully buy or possess an item, speak to an attorney or to the
      <%= jurisdiction.regulator %> before you order.
    </p>

    <h2>Reporting a problem with a listing</h2>
    <p>
      If you believe a listing on this site is inaccurate or should not be offered in your state, tell the
      shop through the <a href="/contact">contact form</a> and it will be reviewed.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>

<%- include('../partials/footer') %>
